 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Sun, 19 Apr 2026 07:22:01 +0100

voice-to-text (2.0.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix: switch to pre-built binary distribution on the PPA.
    Ubuntu LTS cargo 1.75 cannot parse edition-2024 Cargo.toml manifests
    that modern Rust deps use (getrandom 0.3, moxcms, pxfm, toml_edit
    via cpal and arboard). Both 2.0.0 and 2.0.1 failed to build on
    Launchpad for this reason.
  * debian/rules now installs vtt-linux.prebuilt instead of running
    cargo. The binary is compiled locally with Rust 1.91 and committed.
  * Build-Depends reduced to debhelper-compat (= 13) plus runtime libs
    needed by dh_shlibdeps.
  * Source tarball reduced dramatically (vendor/ no longer shipped).
  * Remove notify-rust crate; notifications now shell to notify-send
    from libnotify-bin (added to Depends).
  * When Ubuntu eventually ships rustc 1.85+, this file can revert to
    the cargo-build path at git commit efa5d75.

 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Sun, 19 Apr 2026 06:18:04 +0100

voice-to-text (2.0.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix: pin Cargo.lock to version 3 so Ubuntu Noble's cargo 1.75 can
    parse it (Rust 1.78+ generates version 4 which older cargo rejects).
    The 2.0.0 Launchpad builds failed for exactly this reason.

 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Sun, 19 Apr 2026 03:08:03 +0100

voice-to-text (2.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Rust binary now shipped — 1.0.x releases installed the legacy C binary
    despite the Rust rewrite being in the tree since 1.0.16
  * whisper-rs in-process replaces the CT2 + Python subprocess path — the
    model loads once at startup and remains resident for sub-second
    transcriptions regardless of clip length or model size
  * Python runtime dependency removed (no more python3, python3-pip,
    faster-whisper, or ctranslate2 in the install footprint)
  * Vulkan GPU acceleration on Linux works universally with NVIDIA, AMD,
    and Intel GPUs without requiring the CUDA Toolkit
  * Model menu simplified to a flat list: Small, Medium, Large-v3-turbo,
    Large-v3 — the W/CT2 prefixes are retired along with the dead backends
  * Default model ggml-small.en.bin downloaded via postinst on first install
  * GGML models downloaded on demand from ggerganov/whisper.cpp when users
    select alternatives from the tray menu
  * Breaking: existing CT2 model caches at ~/.cache/huggingface/ are no
    longer used; GGML models re-download on first selection
  * Delete 7,638 lines of obsolete C and Objective-C source
  * See ADR-0003 at CONSCIOUSNESS/adr/0003-*.md for the full architectural
    decision record

